-- JKSSB JE Civil Recruitment 2026: 458 posts (Jal Shakti 282, PWD R&B 176), Advt 11 of 2026 issued 27 October 2026, applications 30 November to 29 December 2026, Pay Level-6 Rs. 35,400-1,12,400, J&K domicile required
-- AEES Teacher Recruitment 2026: 254 posts, Notification 01/2026, last date 22 November 2026 as reported by multiple recruitment reports; official AEES recruitment page checked 28 October 2026 did not list Notification 01/2026, and detailed eligibility/fee/age limits were not in the reports read, so the article states both cautions and directs readers to confirm on aees.gov.in
-- VERIFIED 28 October 2026: TOI + FreeJobAlert + Jagran Josh agree on JKSSB figures; Testbook + Naukri Sanchar + others agree on AEES 254 posts, break-up and 22 November 2026 deadline; live sitemap checked this run, neither slug present.
-- English only per 2026-10-27 article decision: Nepali columns empty strings.
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jkssb-je-civil-458-posts-20261028', 'global', 'India',
'JKSSB JE Civil Recruitment 2026: 458 Posts, Apply from 30 November to 29 December 2026',
'',
'JKSSB has announced 458 Junior Engineer (Civil) posts in Jammu and Kashmir, with online applications opening on 30 November 2026 and closing on 29 December 2026.',
'',
$$<p>The Jammu and Kashmir Services Selection Board (JKSSB) has announced 458 Junior Engineer (Civil) posts in the Jal Shakti Department and the Public Works (R&amp;B) Department, with online applications opening on 30 November 2026 and closing on 29 December 2026. The JKSSB JE Civil recruitment 2026, notified through Advertisement No. 11 of 2026 on 27 October 2026, is one of the largest engineering recruitments the board has opened this year, and it carries a clear domicile condition: applicants must hold a domicile certificate of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir, the Times of India reported.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance: JKSSB JE Civil recruitment 2026</th><th>Detail</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Jammu and Kashmir Services Selection Board (JKSSB)</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Junior Engineer (Civil)</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement number</td><td>11 of 2026, issued on 27 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>458</td></tr><tr><td>Departments</td><td>Jal Shakti Department: 282; Public Works (R&amp;B) Department: 176</td></tr><tr><td>Cadre</td><td>Union Territory cadre</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Pay Level-6, Rs. 35,400 to Rs. 1,12,400</td></tr><tr><td>Applications open</td><td>30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>29 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs. 600 for most categories; Rs. 500 for SC, ST-1, ST-2, EWS and PwBD candidates</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit (Open Merit)</td><td>18 to 40 years, calculated as on 1 January 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Domicile condition</td><td>Valid Jammu and Kashmir domicile certificate required</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Written examination in objective, OMR-based format, followed by document verification</td></tr><tr><td>Written examination date</td><td>Not announced</td></tr><tr><td>Official website</td><td>jkssb.nic.in</td></tr></table>
<h2>JKSSB JE Civil vacancies: 282 posts in Jal Shakti, 176 in Public Works</h2>
<p>The 458 JKSSB JE Civil posts are split between two departments that build and maintain much of the region's everyday infrastructure. The Jal Shakti Department accounts for 282 posts, covering water supply and related civil works, while the Public Works (R&amp;B) Department accounts for 176 posts, covering roads and buildings. The board has stated that the posts fall under the Union Territory cadre, so selected engineers should expect posting anywhere in Jammu and Kashmir rather than in one fixed district, the Times of India reported.</p>
<p>The pay is also fixed in the notification: Pay Level-6, from Rs. 35,400 to Rs. 1,12,400.</p>
<h2>JKSSB JE Civil eligibility: diploma, degree or AMIE, plus domicile</h2>
<p>Three qualification routes lead to the same post. Applicants must hold a three-year Diploma in Civil Engineering from a government-recognised institute, a degree in Civil Engineering from an Indian university, or AMIE Sections A and B, the Times of India reported, with FreeJobAlert and Jagran Josh carrying the same three routes. Candidates whose qualification is in another branch of engineering are not eligible, and the reports warn that certificates in formats other than the prescribed ones can lead to rejection at verification.</p>
<p>The domicile condition deserves emphasis because it decides eligibility before any examination is attempted. The board requires a valid domicile certificate of the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir, and applicants from outside the Union Territory who do not hold one cannot apply, however strong their engineering qualification.</p>
<p>On age, the stated limit for the Open Merit category is 18 to 40 years, calculated as on 1 January 2026. Reserved categories, including SC, ST-1, ST-2, RBA, ALC/IB, EWS and OBC, have a maximum age of 43 years, and physically challenged persons have a maximum of 42 years, according to the recruitment reports. Age relaxation applies under the prescribed rules, so candidates near a boundary should check the category-wise table in the official advertisement rather than relying on the headline figure alone.</p>
<h2>JKSSB JE Civil selection: written examination, then document verification</h2>
<p>Selection rests on a written examination followed by document verification, with no interview stage specified in the reports. The examination will be objective and OMR-based, with questions set in English only, FreeJobAlert reported. Testbook added that one-fourth of the marks assigned to a question will be deducted for each incorrect answer, which makes careful answering more valuable than attempting every question. The written examination date has not been announced, and the board has said it will be notified separately, so applicants should watch jkssb.nic.in after submitting their forms rather than treating any unofficial date as confirmed.</p>
<p>The application fee is Rs. 600 for Open Merit, RBA, OBC, ALC-IB and other categories, and Rs. 500 for SC, ST-1, ST-2, EWS and PwBD candidates, payable online through net banking or debit and credit cards, the reports said. Because applications do not open until 30 November 2026, nobody can submit a form yet, and any person or website claiming to accept applications or fees before that date should not be trusted. The only application route is the board's official website, jkssb.nic.in.</p>
<h2>How to apply for JKSSB JE Civil recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>First, read Advertisement No. 11 of 2026 in full on jkssb.nic.in, including the category-wise vacancy break-up, the prescribed certificate formats and the domicile rules. Second, gather the documents the notification asks for, including the engineering qualification certificate, the domicile certificate, category certificates where applicable, and a recent photograph and signature in the prescribed format. Third, wait for the portal to open on 30 November 2026, fill in the online form, pay the fee for your category, and submit before the deadline of 29 December 2026. Fourth, keep the submitted form and the fee receipt, and check the board's website for the examination date and admit card notice.</p>
<p>For engineers already working in the region's construction and water sectors, the timing matters. The application window opens a full month after the notification, which gives diploma and degree holders time to arrange domicile and category documents, but it closes on 29 December 2026, in the middle of the holiday period, so leaving the form to the final days carries a real risk.</p>
<p>Growentix also covers other Indian government engineering recruitment, including <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bel-probationary-engineer-350-posts-20261028">Bharat Electronics and its 350 probationary engineer posts</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrb-station-master-cen-08-2026-20261026">the Railway Recruitment Board station master recruitment</a>. The JKSSB reporting in this article is drawn from <a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/jkssb-je-civil-recruitment-2026-458-vacancies-announced-applications-open-november-30/articleshow/135249998.cms">the Times of India report on the JKSSB JE Civil notification</a> and <a href="https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/jkssb-junior-engineer-civil-recruitment-2026-3076234">the FreeJobAlert report on the same notification</a>, which agree on the vacancy total, departments, dates, fee and pay.</p>$$, 
