INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'aees-teacher-recruitment-254-posts-20261028', 'global', 'India',
'AEES Teacher Recruitment 2026: 254 Posts, Apply by 22 November 2026',
'',
'AEES has announced 254 teaching and school administration posts across its Atomic Energy Central Schools, with applications closing on 22 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>The Atomic Energy Education Society (AEES) has announced 254 teaching and school administration posts across its Atomic Energy Central Schools, with applications closing on 22 November 2026. The AEES teacher recruitment 2026, issued as Notification No. 01/2026 and reported on 28 October 2026, covers principals, post graduate teachers, trained graduate teachers, librarians, primary teachers and Balvatika teachers, and it is open to Indian citizens, the recruitment reports said.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance: AEES teacher recruitment 2026</th><th>Detail</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Atomic Energy Education Society (AEES)</td></tr><tr><td>Notification number</td><td>01/2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>254</td></tr><tr><td>Posts</td><td>Principal 4; Vice-Principal 1; Post Graduate Teacher 27; Trained Graduate Teacher 102; Librarian 13; Primary Teacher 89; Primary Teacher (Music) 10; Balvatika Teacher 8</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>22 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Online, through the AEES online application panel</td></tr><tr><td>Official website</td><td>aees.gov.in</td></tr><tr><td>Application portal</td><td>aees.onlineregistrationforms.com</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Written examination, followed by interview or skill test where applicable, and document verification</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Not published in the reports read; due on the online panel</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Not published in the reports read; due on the online panel</td></tr><tr><td>Written examination date</td><td>Not announced</td></tr><tr><td>Citizenship condition</td><td>Indian citizens, as reported</td></tr></table>
<h2>AEES teacher vacancies: 254 posts from principal to Balvatika teacher</h2>
<p>The largest share of the AEES teacher recruitment sits in the classroom grades. Trained Graduate Teachers account for 102 posts and Primary Teachers for 89, together making up three-quarters of the total, while Post Graduate Teachers account for 27 posts. The remaining posts are smaller but important for running the schools: 13 librarians, 10 primary teachers for music, 8 Balvatika teachers for the youngest classes, 4 principals and 1 vice-principal, the recruitment reports said. The vacancy total is described as tentative in the advertisement summary, meaning it may increase or decrease, so the final post-wise numbers should be confirmed against the official panel before applying.</p>
<p>AEES runs the Atomic Energy Central Schools attached to the Department of Atomic Energy's establishments, which is why these posts sit in the central government education sector rather than in a state school system. The posting could be at any AEES school in India, not only in the city where the applicant currently lives.</p>
<h2>AEES teacher eligibility: degree, B.Ed. and CTET requirements by post</h2>
<p>Eligibility varies sharply by post, and the headline qualification is not enough on its own. Principals need a master's degree with B.Ed. and teaching or administrative experience, and vice-principals need a master's degree with B.Ed. and teaching experience. Post Graduate Teachers need a master's degree in the relevant subject with B.Ed., while Trained Graduate Teachers need graduation in the relevant subject with B.Ed. and a pass in CTET Paper-II. Primary Teachers need Class 12 with D.El.Ed. or B.El.Ed. and a pass in CTET Paper-I, and Primary Teachers for music need Class 12 with a degree or diploma in music. Balvatika Teachers need Class 12 with a diploma in nursery or early childhood education, and librarians need a degree in library science or graduation with a diploma in library science, the reports said.</p>
<p>Two cautions belong up front. First, the detailed post-wise conditions, including exact age limits, experience requirements and subject-specific combinations, were not published in the reports read; the advertisement summary states that those details will appear on the online application panel, which one report puts on 2 November 2026. Second, the application fee is likewise not stated in the reports read, so no fee figure should be taken from any unofficial page, and anyone asking for payment to secure a post should not be trusted.</p>
<h2>AEES teacher selection: written examination, then interview or skill test</h2>
<p>Selection follows the familiar central school pattern: a written examination, followed by an interview or skill test where applicable for the post, and document verification. The written examination date has not been announced, and admit card and result dates will follow through official announcements, the reports said. Candidates should therefore treat the 22 November 2026 deadline as the only fixed date in the process so far, and watch the official website for everything after it.</p>
<p>On timing, the reports differ on the opening day, and that difference is worth stating plainly rather than smoothing over. Testbook reports that the online application process starts on 29 October 2026, while another report puts the detailed online panel on 2 November 2026. One further caution applies: a check of the official AEES recruitment page on 28 October 2026 did not find Notification No. 01/2026 listed there, although a syllabus for AEES teaching posts dated 26 October 2026 was visible. The figures in this article therefore rest on the agreement of the recruitment reports read, and readers should confirm the notice on aees.gov.in once the panel goes live.</p>
<h2>How to apply for AEES teacher recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>First, open the official AEES website, aees.gov.in, and locate Recruitment Notification No. 01/2026. Second, open the online application panel linked from that notice and read the detailed eligibility, age limit, fee and selection instructions for the chosen post, since those details were not in the first summaries. Third, register on the portal, fill in personal and educational details, upload documents in the prescribed format, and pay any fee the panel states. Fourth, review the form carefully, submit it before 22 November 2026, and save the submitted form and any payment receipt.</p>
<p>For teachers already holding CTET qualification, the AEES window is a central government opening, but the incomplete first summaries make one habit essential: verify every condition on the official panel, not on a summary page.</p>
<p>Growentix also covers other teaching recruitment, including <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/oavs-principals-teachers-815-posts-20261025">Odisha Adarsha Vidyalaya Sangathan recruitment for 815 principal and teacher posts</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/tntet-working-teachers-2026-20261027">the Tamil Nadu teacher eligibility update for working teachers</a>. The AEES reporting in this article is drawn from <a href="https://testbook.com/news/aees-tgt-pgt-prt-recruitment-2026-out/">the Testbook report on the AEES teacher recruitment</a> and <a href="https://naukrisanchar.com/aees-recruitment-2026-254-pgt-tgt-prt-other-posts/">the Naukri Sanchar report on the same notification</a>, which agree on the 254 vacancies, the post break-up and the 22 November 2026 deadline.</p>$$, 
'',
